    "result_text": "Tests are green. \n\nI agreed with the finding \u2014 it's exactly the `BusinessDays` idiom this codebase already uses for the per-day rule pair. I extracted a `CityCapacity` helper that owns the single definition of \"owners in a city\" plus the `CITY_CAPACITY` and `WARNING_THRESHOLD` constants:\n\n- **`CityCapacity.java`** (new) \u2014 `countInCity(OwnerRepository, String)` and the `CITY_CAPACITY = 50` / `WARNING_THRESHOLD = 40` constants, mirroring `BusinessDays`.\n- **`EnsureCityCapacity`** \u2014 now counts via `CityCapacity.countInCity` and rejects at `CityCapacity.CITY_CAPACITY`; dropped its private constant and the inline stream.\n- **`AssessCityCapacity`** \u2014 now counts via the same helper and warns on `[WARNING_THRESHOLD, CITY_CAPACITY)`; dropped its duplicated constants and stream.\n\nThe hard-limit and warning halves are now anchored to one definition of the matching rule, so a future change (case-insensitive match, excluding soft-deleted owners, etc.) applies to both by construction. Acceptance behaviour is unchanged and `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
